## H1: AI Team Training

Handing your team a login to an AI tool isn't training — it's a guessing game. Most teams end up either avoiding AI altogether or using it in ways that create real risk: inaccurate content, compliance gaps, or a loss of the voice that makes your organization trustworthy.

Guiding Point Consulting delivers **hands-on AI training for nonprofit and government contractor teams** — practical sessions built around the actual tools and actual content your people work with every day, not generic AI 101.

### What You Get

- Live, hands-on training sessions tailored to your team's actual workflows — not a canned webinar
- Clear guidance on where AI genuinely helps (drafting, research, first-pass summaries) and where it shouldn't be trusted unsupervised
- Simple, repeatable guardrails your team can use on their own after training ends
- Optional follow-up support as your team builds confidence and adjusts their workflow

### Who This Is For

- **Nonprofits** whose staff are curious about AI but unsure how to use it without risking accuracy or donor trust
- **Government prime contractors** who need their subcontracted or internal teams trained on responsible AI use that meets compliance expectations
- Leadership teams who want AI adoption to be intentional, not accidental

### What This Is Not

This isn't a one-hour "here's ChatGPT" demo. It's structured training built around your organization's real content, real compliance needs, and real risk tolerance.

### The Outcome

A team that uses AI confidently and correctly — faster first drafts, fewer bottlenecks, and none of the credibility risk that comes from careless AI use.

**Investment:** AI Team Training is scoped to your team size and goals — reach out for a custom quote.

